> Conclusion

Fourteen recorded TensorFlow selection fixtures, group separation, colliding assignments, anchor geometry, 1000 Float64 coding round trips and zero-logit loss derivatives are checked. The visible Adam fixture verifies paired parameter/state restoration and strict validation ties. These synthetic checks establish mechanics; dataset detection quality is measured in the architecture reports.

> References

- [TensorFlow, tf.image.non_max_suppression](https://www.tensorflow.org/api_docs/python/tf/image/non_max_suppression).
- [Ren et al. (2015), Faster R-CNN](https://arxiv.org/abs/1506.01497).
- [Liu et al. (2016), SSD: Single Shot MultiBox Detector](https://arxiv.org/abs/1512.02325).
